{
  "$comment": "Design system of the graph explorer page (FTR-TRC-014; ADR-TRC-025: DEC-TRC-084, DEC-TRC-091; structure of ADR-TRC-002: DEC-TRC-009, DEC-TRC-010, RQ-TRC-018). Three tiers, as the performance center's: global holds the only raw values; semantic names a role and refers to a global token; component refers to a semantic token. graph.py writes semantic tokens as --s-<name> and component tokens as --c-<name>; the page's CSS and script use those only. The values are copied from agnos-perf-center/assets/tokens.json (owner's option A, 2026-11-23: no file shared between the two skills), light theme only (FTR-TRC-014 leaves a dark theme out). Node types keep the performance center's surfaces (Okabe-Ito hues for FTR to TASK, indigo for functions, slate for files, red for undefined IDs) and gain one type-*-text token each (DEC-TRC-091), a darker shade of the same hue reaching at least 4.5:1 on surface, surface-subtle and surface-selected (RQ-TRC-157): measured 4.76 (FTR, the Okabe-Ito blue itself) to 9.51 (sections). Sections (SEC), absent from the performance center, take slate-500 as surface and slate-700 as text. The AGNOS brand mark of the header (owner's request of 2026-11-23, TASK-TRC-134) keeps the five colours of the performance center's brand tokens (RQ-TRC-114, DEC-TRC-056). The graph view (RQ-TRC-150, DEC-TRC-090) keeps the performance center's zoom bounds and wheel sensitivity; its zoom step (1.25 per click), its column layout (a column per type, 220 graph units apart, 56 between rows, wrapped every 40 nodes), the label's smallest zoomed size (8) the fit padding (24) and the spacing of an isolated neighbourhood's circles (40) are its own, in graph units, not CSS pixels. A table column is resized down to 48 px at least, by a handle 6 px wide on its header's right edge (RQ-TRC-159). The graph legend draws each relation kind as a line 24 px long, in the kind's edge colour (RQ-TRC-165). A graph node's hover tooltip opens after 1000 ms, the performance center's duration.tooltip, and is at most as wide as the detail panel's default width (RQ-TRC-167). The help dialog, its licence badges and its About lockup (FTR-GXP-001: RQ-GXP-002 to RQ-GXP-004; DEC-GXP-002) copy the performance center's values: the dialog 960 by 680 px, at least 480 by 320 px; badges 24 px high, label slate-600 on white ink, value slate-950 on the brand tone of the licence, semibold; the wordmark 30 px bold with 0.12em tracking and 1.1 line height, the tagline with 0.02em tracking and 1.3 line height; the large mark 96 px. The time bar (RQ-GXP-006, DEC-GXP-003) draws a track 4 px high in border-strong, the selected period filled with the accent, and two round handles 14 px wide in the accent ringed by the surface; these sizes are its own. The playback (RQ-GXP-007, DEC-GXP-006) offers three speeds, 2, 7 and 30 days of history per second, 7 by default; its cursor is drawn as a 2 px line in the text colour across the track. The time track shares the controls' row and wraps under them below 120 px (TASK-GXP-009). While a handle of the time bar is dragged, the views wait until it rests 400 ms or is released (TASK-GXP-010). The 3D view (RQ-GXP-011, DEC-GXP-008, DEC-GXP-009; TASK-GXP-013) places its points in a cylinder 100 world units wide and high, draws each point 6 CSS pixels wide whatever the zoom, rotates by 0.005 radian per dragged pixel, and opens with a 50 degree field of view at 3 times that extent from its centre, on the 2D view's background and zoom bounds; these values are its own. A 3D point is picked within 8 CSS pixels of the pointer (RQ-GXP-012, DEC-GXP-010; TASK-GXP-014). A point's size dimension scales it from 0.5 to 2 times its size, and a numeric colour dimension goes from the 2D view's edge colour to the accent (RQ-GXP-013, DEC-GXP-011; TASK-GXP-015). The month rings and the cursor's grid plane are drawn in border-strong, their labels as the graph's labels (RQ-GXP-015, DEC-GXP-013; TASK-GXP-017). The axis indicator is a square of 96 CSS pixels in the bottom left corner, and the cartesian trihedron is graduated in 4 intervals; their x, y and z axes take the Okabe-Ito vermillion, green and blue, the usual red, green and blue of axes (RQ-GXP-020, RQ-GXP-021, DEC-GXP-014, DEC-GXP-015; TASK-GXP-020 to TASK-GXP-022).",
